/></figure></div><hr class="section-divider"/><p data-text-role="note"><em>Firaaq is a scholar of human rights and an independent journalist based in New Delhi. His work has appeared in publications like NewClick<sup class="cite-ref">[1]</sup>, GroundXero<sup class="cite-ref">[2]</sup>, and Nutan Charcha.</em></p></div></div></div></div><div class="page" data-page="3" style="page:p3;width:210.0mm;height:297.0mm;position:relative;margin:0 auto 12px;box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.3);"><div class="dtp-block" data-block-id="18fed02d" data-page="3" style="left:0mm;top:0mm;width:210.0mm;height:297.0mm;"><div style="width:100%;height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;background:var(--paper);padding:15.0mm 18.0mm 15.0mm 18.0mm;overflow:hidden"><div class="art-content dropcap" style="counter-reset:ve-sec 0"><p data-text-role="note"><em>Mouli Sharma<sup class="cite-ref">[3]</sup> is an independent journalist and illustrator from New Delhi. Her work has appeared in publications like Maktoob Media<sup class="cite-ref">[4]</sup>, GroundXero<sup class="cite-ref">[5]</sup>, The Observer Post<sup class="cite-ref">[6]</sup>, The Leaflet<sup class="cite-ref">[7]</sup>,Nivarana<sup class="cite-ref">[8]</sup>,The Polis Project<sup class="cite-ref">[9]</sup>,Article 14<sup class="cite-ref">[10]</sup>,Feminism in India<sup class="cite-ref">[11]</sup>, and been republished in SabrangIndia<sup class="cite-ref">[12]</sup>, NewsClick<sup class="cite-ref">[13]</sup> andThink Global Health<sup class="cite-ref">[14]</sup>. She is a published photojournalist &amp; illustrator and has been featured in theHindu College Gazette<sup class="cite-ref">[15]</sup> and the quarterly Pink Disco<sup class="cite-ref">[16]</sup>. She is the editor-in-chief of the student-run news site, The Voice Express<sup class="cite-ref">[17]</sup>, and is a literary editor for the digital lit-mag, The Queer Gaze<sup class="cite-ref">[18]</sup>.</em></p></div></div></div></div><div class="page" data-page="4" style="page:p4;wi